      {
        "id": 122305,
        "name": "danmarshall14",
        "username": "danmarshall14",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/danmarshall14/{size}/1944_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-09T08:57:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Overall, Shattered Timelines.</p><p>I love La Capitan and Iron Legacy; they're up there as my top favorite Villains of all time. &nbsp;The Dreamer and Kismet also offer two pretty different approaches to fighting a villain, which rounds out the expansion quite well.</p><p>Hero-wise, OX and Chrono Ranger are always fun to play, decently strong when they get rolling, and easy for anyone in my gaming group to understand right off the bat.</p><p>On the environment front, these aren't my top picks. &nbsp;The Block is pretty fun, mostly because it's incredibly unpunishing, making it a great beginning environment for new players and I love the theme. &nbsp;But Time Cataclysm has always bored me, at least thematically, since it's just a mashup of other environments.</p><p>As a whole though, Shattered Timelines is an awesome package and offers a perfect spectrum of approachability to complexity. &nbsp;There's something in this pack for veterans and newbies alike.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:56:01.375Z",
