      {
        "id": 122308,
        "name": "Katsue",
        "username": "Katsue",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/katsue/{size}/2012_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-13T14:11:19.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"danmarshall14\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/danmarshall14/48/1944_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> danmarshall14:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The Block is pretty fun, mostly because it's incredibly unpunishing, making it a great beginning environment for new players and I love the theme. &nbsp;But Time Cataclysm has always bored me, at least thematically, since it's just a mashup of other environments.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Mechanically speaking, Time Cataclysm is a much better Environment than The Block (or the Final Wasteland, or the Mobile Defence Platform), though.</p>",
