      {
        "id": 122309,
        "name": "Sefirit",
        "username": "Sefirit",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/e68b1a/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-13T16:09:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"SSJ3Godzilla\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/db5fbb/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> SSJ3Godzilla:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Vengeance has some amazing heroes and I like both environments, but the vengeful five usually don't hit the table because my group feels they take to long and are fiddly.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>My group isn't a fan of the Vengeful Five either. &nbsp;Vengence is my least favorite expansion. The heroes in it are really fun, but the villain thing never did it for me. &nbsp;I know that is strictly a personal preference so I would never argue that it is bad, just not for me. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>In addition, I find the environments in Vengence to be terrible. Not terrible in the Rook City unforgiving way, more like 7 rounds into a game with Mobile Defense Platform before you even realize you chose to play an environment. &nbsp;I've had a bunch of games where all MDP does is prevent damage to itself and heal itself have some random structure in play that don't affect the game. &nbsp;Its become a big joke for us that if you don't want to play an environment just play MDP.</p>\n<p>On the other hand Freedom Tower is the reverse of Rook City, I think every card except for the one with Fright Train breaking a hole in the wall benefits players greatly. &nbsp;I expect both of these to be jumping up the charts of easiest environments.</p>\n<p>So heroes aside, it wasn't a great expansion for me. &nbsp;Compare that with Infernal Relics, which is may favorite. IR had two of my favorite heroes, but just due to volume I'd give the edge to Vengence. &nbsp;Tomb and Realm were both interesting environments. &nbsp;You definitely felt their presence. &nbsp;They could be hard, but not Rook City or Atlantis hard. &nbsp;Overall good environments so check. &nbsp;The villains in IR were good to. &nbsp;Enead was very interesting and different and fun. &nbsp;I thought they were all good, except generally too easy. &nbsp;That was the only drawback to IR, that the villains were often easy.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
