        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nal0781/{size}/2041_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-15T23:49:07.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Infernal Relics would have to be my Number 1. &nbsp;Probably my favorite set of villains. &nbsp;I especially enjoy Apostate and the Ennead. &nbsp;Also, maybe my two favorite environments (of those released. &nbsp;The Tomb is fun but can be brutal. &nbsp;The Realm changes things up often but is usually manageable in terms of upkeep. &nbsp;Alrhough I like bot Argent Adept and Nightmist, they are middle heroes for me in terms of my preference and less popular with my gaming group.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Rook City would have to be my choice for heroes. &nbsp;Two of my favorites. &nbsp;Mr Fixed never ceases to amaze me and thematically Expatriette may be my favorite (along with Setback. Environments are hard but okay but I am not a huge fan of the villains. &nbsp;Chairman and Matriarch are too difficult and I don't like Spite for character reasons.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>i am a fan of the Vengeance heroes. &nbsp;I actially love the new villain style, unfortunately my group does not. &nbsp;And it is a little much to keep track of solo so unfortunately they hardly get played. &nbsp;Unfortunately the Environments just didn't do it for me.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Finally Shattered Timelines. &nbsp;Still a solid expansion - just ranks fourth. &nbsp;Villains are right there with IR. &nbsp;I love Dreamer and La Capitan. &nbsp;Kismet is decent. &nbsp;Iron Legacy is not my style. &nbsp;While I have nothing against either hero, they aren't really my play style. &nbsp;Both environments were awesome when I first played them, but for me they don't quite stand up.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Mini expansions are great also, but I will not get into them here. &nbsp;I do love all of the expansions but if I had ranked them, the above would be my order.</p>",
        "post_number": 29,
        "post_type": 1,
